<https://hse-oahwb-profile.adaptcentre.ie/indicator/hse0000075> a dcat:Dataset,
        :Indicator ;
    healthdcatap:healthTheme "DEMOGRAPHICS" ;
    dcterms:identifier "hse0000075" ;
    dcterms:provenance "CSO - Population and Labour Force Projections" ;
    dcterms:title "Projected Dependency Ratios from 2022" ;
    skos:definition "Estimates showing the possible future number of people aged 65 years and over, compared to those of working age, used to plan future services. Dependency ratio: The dependency ratio is a demographic indicator that compares the number of people considered to be dependents (too young or too old to be in the workforce) to the number of people considered to be in the working-age population. It essentially measures the burden on the working population to support the non-working age groups ( can be calculated by adding people aged 0-15 to those aged 65+ and dividing the whole lot by people aged 16-64 years)" ;
    :numeratorSource "https://data.cso.ie/table/PEC22" ;
    :status "Include in Delphi" .

